      "description": "Watch Ajax Amsterdam vs FC Sion highlights and goals from UEFA Europa Conference League on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 27, 2026. The stage was set at the Johan Cruyff Arena for a fascinating encounter as Ajax Amsterdam hosted FC Sion in the UEFA Conference League . On August 27, 2026, fans gathered expecting a high-intensity battle, and both sides looked to assert their dominance early in what would become a rollercoaster of momentum shifts. Explosive First Half Action The match ignited within seconds of the kickoff. Youri Baas found the back of the net in the 1st minute following a precise assist from Steven Berghuis , giving Ajax a dream start. However, FC Sion responded valiantly through the brilliance of Winsley Boteli . The young forward silenced the home crowd by equalizing in the 19th minute and then stunning the stadium again in the 36th minute to put the visitors ahead. The lead was short-lived, as Davy Klaassen restored parity for the hosts just three minutes later, finishing a move started by Lucas Rosa . Ajax Take Control Before the Break As the first half drew to a close, Ajax ramped up the pressure. In the first minute of stoppage time, Tolu Arokodare struck to put the Amsterdam giants back in front, thanks to a well-timed pass from Abdellah Ouazane . The momentum stayed with the home side as the second half began. Arokodare secured his brace in the 51st minute, before substitute Oliver Edvardsen extended the lead to 5-2 shortly after, capitalizing on an assist from Caio Henrique . A Late Consolidation Despite a flurry of substitutions from both managers, including the introduction of Marcos Leonardo and Oscar Gloukh for the hosts, the scoring wasn't over. While Ajax seemed comfortable, FC Sion continued to push, and Winsley Boteli managed to complete his hat-trick in the 91st minute. The final whistle blew shortly after, concluding a breathtaking 5-3 contest that showcased clinical finishing and relentless attacking football from both participants."
